title: "The Mitochondrial Disclosure Surface: An Atlas of VDAC1, Cardiolipin, and the Sensitization Axis"
abstract: >-
  A working synthesis, developed across multiple model architectures in a
  research relay, recasting the outer mitochondrial membrane as an active
  disclosure surface rather than a passive permeability barrier. Mitochondrial
  state is continuously published into the cytosol through the lipid-protein
  interface of the outer membrane, with the class and bandwidth of disclosure
  set by a high-dimensional physical state vector. VDAC1 is repositioned as a
  central witness-node, a high-bandwidth readout and effector hub defined by its
  partner network, rather than a sovereign decider of cellular fate. The v0.3
  sequential-sensitization spine proposes VDAC1 oligomerization as a single
  upstream axis whose amplitude and duration determine whether stress resolves
  as metabolic exchange, mitophagic containment, an inflammatory mtDNA alarm via
  cGAS-STING, or apoptotic commitment through BAX/BAK macropores. A falsifiable
  multiplexed experiment distinguishing this spine from the parallel-attractor
  alternative is proposed; four load-bearing literature claims carry
  verification-status flags.
